== fm-control-relaunch
ok - fm-control relaunch: a secondmate's child work is accounted for and its charter is left alone
ok - fm-control relaunch: a secondmate home that is not this secondmate's is refused
ok - fm-control relaunch: unreadable child records fail checkpoint
ok - fm-control relaunch: unlistable state check skipped as root (mode 000 does not restrict root)
ok - fm-control relaunch: a vanished watcher scratch file does not fail the child-record checkpoint
ok - fm-control relaunch: two control actions on one task serialize instead of interleaving
ok - fm-spawn relaunch: direct entry participates in lifecycle serialization
ok - fm-promote: promotion participates in lifecycle serialization
ok - fm-spawn --relaunch: refuses to launch a second agent into a live endpoint
ok - fm-spawn --relaunch: symlinked records refuse before inspection
ok - fm-spawn --relaunch: keeps its early meta lock continuous
ok - fm-spawn --relaunch: pending closes refuse before replacement begins
ok - fm-spawn --relaunch: every identity axis comes from the record, and a contradicting flag refuses
ok - fm-spawn --relaunch: an unrecorded task is refused
ok - fm-spawn --relaunch: refuses to start a replacement outside the copy holding its work
ok - tmux: a window absent from its session refuses both verbs rather than being assumed gone
ok - tmux: an unfindable session refuses both verbs, so a live agent is never duplicated
ok - tmux: a dead server on this socket refuses both verbs rather than proving absence
ok - tmux: a window missing under a changed boot identity is re-created in its worktree and the record rebinds
ok - tmux: an unchanged boot identity keeps the refusal on both verbs
ok - tmux: a record with no boot identity keeps the refusal on both verbs
ok - tmux: a platform with no readable boot identity keeps the refusal on both verbs
ok - reclaim: an unclassifiable endpoint is still refused, so two agents cannot share one
